                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Including E Mercier aand B mercier. See Ed Pope: See also Mercier, B
                            which could have been the same person. Elizabeth Benigna Mercier =
                            Daniel Dowling 1814 St Pancras. Dowling was an Irish schoolmaster and
                            author of books on mathematics. He was bankrupt at Devonshire-st
                            Queen-sq in 1813, then master of Mansion House Academy, Highgate till
                            1818, moved to Upper Mall Hammersmith, and to Dublin by 1838. Their
                            daughter Fanny Elizabeth died 1828 age 13. Charles Hutton son of Daniel
                            and Elizabeth Dowling bapt St Pancras 1822. Her second entry above is the
                            eve of Louisa Mercier's wedding to Holcroft. See also Marshall, Mrs for
                            EM entries in 1804 and 1806. </p>
                    </note>
